+</style><main><section class="panel" id="world-answer-quality-r1"><h1>World Answer Quality &amp; Customer Experience Closure R1</h1><p><strong>HUMAN_REVIEW · 本地候选，未发布 / Local candidate, not released</strong></p><p>上一轮交互方向的有条件接受保留；旧 8 PARTIAL / 2 MISSING 及负面记录保持原样。本轮采用“直接解释所问机制／有依据事实／有用比较方法／个人条件与下一步”的标准，不按有无地区数值一刀切。</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/world/?locale=zh-Hans">实际 World 中文</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/world/?locale=en">World English</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/L1/PRODUCT-LOCAL.html?locale=zh-Hans">中文：问题到 Reality</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/L1/PRODUCT-LOCAL.html?locale=en">English: question to Reality</a></p><p>本轮预览59834，保留旧59833。启动：<code>node --import ./scripts/lib/pages-json-import-preload.mjs tools/review/reality-information-contract-r1/L1/server.mjs --serve</code></p><h2>先体验 / Try the product</h2><p>自己输入公共问题 → 先读回答、原因条件和下一步 → 从论点旁 [1] 查看具体依据 → 在下方“我的问题”写当前情况与两个方向 → 明确同意本次会话 → 比较并作自己的选择 → 记录之后实际发生什么 → 复核 → 刷新 → 撤销清空。当前情况填写完成后折叠，空的资料区不再重复警告。没有自动保存，也没有编造关系或行动历史。</p><p><strong>工程逐题阅读判定：原十题中英20答均有直接有用的机制／方法回答；第8题只通过比较方法，不代表已经取到国家差异数据。这个门槛不代表更广泛开放问答通过，Human 最终判定仍待完成。</strong></p><p>额外十题首次留出结果：12 直接、7 部分、1 数值受限；通用词汇与投影修复后同题复测：14 直接、2 部分、4 数值受限。首次结果保留，复测不冒充新盲测。地铁与租金的因果解释、真实马来西亚房贷拒绝率、两国制造业就业观测仍有明确缺口。</p><h2>原十题修改前后 / Before and after</h2><article><h3>1. 燃油与运输成本 / 能源、化肥与食品生产 / 零售传递的条件和时滞</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 油价上涨后，为什么连买菜和送货也可能变贵？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 全球化重新加速，需要运输标准、能源与制度同时支持。集装箱降低跨运输方式的转换成本，石油则为交通、工业与全球物流提供高密度能源，使远距离生产网络能够持续扩展。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT: existing globalization/oil material establishes energy-logistics context, not food-price pass-through.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 油价上涨不只影响加油：燃油变贵会推高运输成本，能源和化肥成本也会进入食品生产，因而买菜和送货都可能变贵。</p><p>食品经过生产和运输才到家庭；这些环节的投入成本上升，可能逐步传到零售价。</p><p>传递不一定即时或等比例：补贴、存货和当地供需条件会改变家庭实际承受的涨幅。</p><p>这里解释传递机制，不预测当地物价或把石油与天然气当作同一种商品。</p><ol><li>对照同一时期的燃油、食品和配送账单，不把全部涨价都归因于石油。</li><li>如要估计本地涨幅，再查当地价格篮子、补贴及运输成本资料。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 本地传递幅度、时滞和补贴覆盖尚未估计。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2022/12/09/global-food-prices-to-remain-elevated-amid-war-costly-energy-la-nina">Energy costs and food prices</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/Blogs/Articles/2022/04/28/blog-africa-faces-new-shock-as-war-raises-food-fuel-costs">Africa Faces New Shock as War Raises Food and Fuel Costs</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · Why can rising oil costs make groceries and deliveries more expensive?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> The reacceleration of globalization depended on transport standards, energy and institutions working together. Containerization reduced transfer costs across transport modes, while oil supplied dense energy for mobility, industry and logistics, allowing long-distance production networks to expand.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT: existing globalization/oil material establishes energy-logistics context, not food-price pass-through.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> Oil affects more than the fuel bill: dearer fuel raises transport costs, while energy and fertilizer costs enter food production. Groceries and deliveries can therefore become more expensive.</p><p>Food reaches households through production and transport; higher input costs can gradually reach retail prices.</p><p>Pass-through need not be immediate or proportional: subsidies, inventories and local supply and demand affect what households actually pay.</p><p>This explains channels, not local price forecasts; oil and natural gas are distinct commodities.</p><ol><li>Compare fuel, food and delivery bills for the same period; do not attribute every price rise to oil.</li><li>For local magnitudes, obtain the relevant price basket, subsidy and transport-cost data.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Local pass-through magnitude, timing and subsidy coverage are not estimated.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2022/12/09/global-food-prices-to-remain-elevated-amid-war-costly-energy-la-nina">Energy costs and food prices</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/Blogs/Articles/2022/04/28/blog-africa-faces-new-shock-as-war-raises-food-fuel-costs">Africa Faces New Shock as War Raises Food and Fuel Costs</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>2. 总产出不等于每人工资 / 收入分配与税后可用收入 / 名义工资与购买力</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 工资没涨，经济增长的数据对家庭有什么意义？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 发展主义把经济增长、工业能力与国家建设连接起来，国家工业化则把资本、产业与基础设施集中到长期转型目标。相似工具在不同社会却产生不同结果。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT in English; BACKGROUND_ONLY in Chinese developmentalism passage. Wage distribution and purchasing power were not established.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> GDP 增长表示全社会产出增加，不表示每个家庭工资都会增加。家庭是否更宽裕，要看自己的税后收入、收入分配和必要支出的价格。</p><p>平均工资可以在部分高收入者加薪时上升，其他人未必获得同样增幅；总量和平均数都不能代替你的工资。</p><p>即使名义收入增加，物价上涨也可能抵消购买力；还应区分税前工资与税后可用收入。</p><p>没有据此判断某个国家当年工资或每个家庭的实际变化。</p><ol><li>对照同一时期的实得收入与食品、住房、交通支出。</li><li>看典型家庭时优先查收入中位数、实际可支配收入及其覆盖人群。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 具体国家、年份及家庭分组的收入与价格数据仍需另查。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/datasets/gdp-and-non-financial-accounts.html">GDP and Non-financial Accounts</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/indicators/average-annual-wages.html">Average annual wages</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · What does economic growth mean for a household whose wages have not risen?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT in English; BACKGROUND_ONLY in Chinese developmentalism passage. Wage distribution and purchasing power were not established.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> GDP growth means greater total output, not a pay rise for every household. Whether a family is better off depends on its disposable income, distribution of gains and the prices of necessities.</p><p>Average wages can rise when gains are concentrated among higher earners; totals and averages do not describe your own pay.</p><p>Even a nominal pay rise can be offset by prices. Gross wages must also be distinguished from disposable income.</p><p>No claim is made about wages in a particular country-year or every family.</p><ol><li>Compare take-home income and food, housing and transport costs over the same period.</li><li>For typical households, seek median and real disposable income with clear population coverage.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Country-year and household-group income and price data must be queried separately.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/datasets/gdp-and-non-financial-accounts.html">GDP and Non-financial Accounts</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/indicators/average-annual-wages.html">Average annual wages</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>3. 收益征收管理 / 公共投资和本地联系 / 波动与产业多样化</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 矿产很多的地方，为什么就业和公共服务仍然薄弱？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 目前能核验的资料还不足以解释这个问题。先明确你想了解的变化、地点或比较对象，再找对应资料；我不会用不相关的例子代替。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> MISSING: no admitted supporting paragraph.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 地下有资源不等于居民已经富裕。资源必须形成可获得的收入，再通过税收、公共投资和本地产业联系转化为就业与服务；这些环节失灵时，开采繁荣也可能没有带动多数家庭。</p><p>收益如何征收、管理并投入教育、健康和基础设施，影响资源财富能否扩散到居民。</p><p>只依赖开采还会暴露于商品价格起落；发展本地供应链和其他产业，是减少这种依赖的方向，并非保证成功。</p><p>依据非洲资源发展研究解释可能机制，不把资源丰富等同于腐败，也不诊断某个国家。</p><ol><li>查资源税收去了哪里，以及本地采购、就业和公共服务的实际变化。</li><li>再比较教育、基础设施和非开采产业投入，而不只比较矿产储量。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 特定国家的合同、财政、地方就业和服务数据尚未核对。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2023/05/09/maximizing-revenues-from-natural-resource-wealth-could-yield-big-fiscal-and-environmental-dividends-for-african-countrie">Resource revenues and local development</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · Why can a mineral-rich place still have weak jobs and public services?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> The currently verifiable material is not enough to explain this question. Specify the change, place or comparison you want to understand so the next source can be selected; an unrelated example will not replace your question.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> MISSING: no admitted supporting paragraph.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> Resources underground do not automatically make residents prosperous. Revenues must be captured and converted into public investment and local economic links; extraction can expand without broad gains when those links fail.</p><p>How rents are collected, managed and invested in health, education and infrastructure affects whether residents benefit.</p><p>Dependence on extraction exposes economies to commodity cycles. Local value chains and diversification can reduce reliance, without guaranteeing success.</p><p>The Africa research illustrates possible channels; resource wealth does not establish corruption or diagnose a particular country.</p><ol><li>Trace resource revenue and observed local procurement, employment and services.</li><li>Compare investment in people, infrastructure and non-extractive sectors, not reserves alone.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Country-specific contracts, fiscal flows, local jobs and services are not assessed.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2023/05/09/maximizing-revenues-from-natural-resource-wealth-could-yield-big-fiscal-and-environmental-dividends-for-african-countrie">Resource revenues and local development</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>4. 任务而非整职业 / 暴露与实际采用/裁员分开 / 观察真实岗位及技能变化</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 如果企业开始用人工智能，我应该观察哪些就业变化？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 这里不宣称平台已经成为国家，也不假设人工智能必然取代人类治理。关键是观察哪些功能正在迁移、哪些决定需要可申诉与人类责任，以及快速模型如何保持可检查和可纠正。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> BACKGROUND_ONLY: AI governance does not establish employment-task effects.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 先观察工作里的任务如何改变，而不是把使用 AI 等同于岗位消失。同一职业中，有些任务可被自动化，有些仍需人来判断、沟通或完成；岗位可能因此重组。</p><p>技术上可处理任务，不等于企业已经采用，也不等于实际裁员；技能、成本和基础设施会影响采用。</p><p>这是任务变化的分析方法，不预测你的岗位是否被裁，也不把暴露度当失业率。</p><ol><li>列出每周任务，标出可自动处理、需人工复核和必须现场完成的部分。</li><li>对照企业实际流程、培训和招聘要求，再选择一个具体技能补齐。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 行业、岗位任务及企业实际采用和招聘变化尚待核对。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.ilo.org/resource/article/how-might-generative-ai-impact-different-occupations">How might generative AI impact different occupations?</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · If firms adopt artificial intelligence, what employment changes should I watch?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> Technology&#x27;s deepest contribution to expansion is not the removal of cost, but the compression of high-cost processes into lower-cost repeatable structures. Communication compresses distance, records compress memory cost, standards compress negotiation, automation compresses repeated execution, and computation compresses the human attention required to scan large state spaces.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> BACKGROUND_ONLY: AI governance does not establish employment-task effects.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> Watch changes in tasks before equating AI adoption with disappearing jobs. Some tasks can be automated while others still need people; a job can be reorganized rather than eliminated.</p><p>Technical task exposure is not actual adoption or observed layoffs; skills, costs and infrastructure affect implementation.</p><p>This is a task-analysis method, not a layoff prediction; exposure is not an unemployment rate.</p><ol><li>List weekly tasks and distinguish automation, human review and on-site work.</li><li>Check actual workflows, training and job requirements before choosing a specific skill to develop.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Sector, task mix and observed firm adoption and hiring must be checked.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.ilo.org/resource/article/how-might-generative-ai-impact-different-occupations">How might generative AI impact different occupations?</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>5. 照护需求 / 实际参与和健康退休安排 / 不推出必然衰退</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 老年人口增加会如何改变家庭照护和劳动供给？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 人口压缩首先发生在年龄、能力与责任结构，而不是总人口数字。年轻节点减少、老年节点增加，会重新安排劳动、照顾、财政与知识更新之间的关系。当前经济与城市仍然可以依靠既有成年人、资本和技术维持，但真正变化的是未来节点进入速度：越来越多能力被用于维护已经形成的结构，能够投入下一阶段的余量逐渐下降。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> DIRECT_SUPPORT for some demographic mechanisms; local scale and public-source grounding were incomplete.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 老年人口比重上升，会同时改变需要照护的人数与能够投入工作的时间和人力。养老金、医疗和长期照护需求可能增加；实际劳动力变化仍取决于健康、退休安排与劳动参与。</p><p>不能只按年龄判定不能工作；健康改善和更高参与可以缓解劳动力压力，但不会自动解决所有照护与财政问题。</p><p>不同地区退休制度和健康状况不同，不能推出所有老龄社会都会衰退。</p><ol><li>写出家庭照护时段、可用服务和谁能分担。</li><li>再核对工作弹性、照护服务可得性及当地劳动参与资料。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 本地年龄结构、劳动参与与照护服务能力仍需数据。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.elibrary.imf.org/display/book/9798400289583/CH002.xml">Population ageing, work and care</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · How can an older population change family care and labour supply?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> Population compression begins in the structure of age, capability, and responsibility rather than in the headline population number. Fewer younger nodes and more older nodes rearrange labor, care, public finance, and knowledge renewal. The economy and cities may continue to function through existing adults, capital, and technology, while the real change occurs in the inflow of future nodes: more present capability is used to maintain what already exists, leaving less surplus for the next stage.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> DIRECT_SUPPORT for some demographic mechanisms; local scale and public-source grounding were incomplete.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> An older population changes care demand and the people and time available for work. Pension, health and long-term care needs can grow, while labour supply still depends on health, retirement and participation.</p><p>Age alone does not establish inability to work. Better health and participation can ease labour pressures without automatically resolving care and fiscal needs.</p><p>Retirement institutions and health differ; ageing does not establish inevitable decline everywhere.</p><ol><li>List care hours, available services and who can share responsibility.</li><li>Check flexible work, care-service availability and local participation data.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Local age structure, participation and care capacity require data.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.elibrary.imf.org/display/book/9798400289583/CH002.xml">Population ageing, work and care</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>6. 分别解释水、电和港口 / 连接、持续供应与中断成本 / 具体厂址条件</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 为什么工厂选址要同时考虑用水、港口和供电？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 机器不会自动产生工厂。动力、设备、原料、劳动与管理需要在同一地点持续协调，才使集中生产成为一种组织方式。工厂改变的不只是生产地点，也是人们共同使用时间的方法。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT: factory organization alone does not separately explain water, power and ports.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 工业选址要同时看水、电和物流，因为生产投入、设备运行和货物流通必须衔接；其中一个环节不可靠，都可能使整个生产安排受阻。</p><p>水：要核对所需水量、水质、持续供应和排水条件；没有符合工艺要求的水源，低地价也未必可用。</p><p>电：要看供电容量和稳定性，而不只看标价；停电可能迫使产线停工。</p><p>港口与物流：要看与供应商和客户的连接、运输时间及可靠性；港口延误会拖慢原料到达和产品交付。</p><p>这是可行性核对方法，不是具体厂址批准或投资建议。</p><ol><li>按拟生产产品列出水、电和交付时间要求。</li><li>用各候选地的供应记录、接入条件和物流报价逐项比较。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 具体工艺、环境许可、水电记录和路线成本未核对。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://ipp.unido.org/industrial-parks-guidelines/phase-two-planning-design-and-policy-framework">Phase two - Feasibility studies</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://documents.worldbank.org/curated/en/336371560797230631/pdf/Underutilized-Potential-The-Business-Costs-of-Unreliable-Infrastructure-in-Developing-Countries.pdf">Infrastructure reliability and production</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/transport/how-resilient-ports-can-mitigate-global-supply-chain-disruptions">How resilient ports can mitigate global supply chain disruptions</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · Why does factory location depend on water, ports and electricity together?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> Machines do not automatically create factories. Power, equipment, materials, labor and management must be coordinated continuously in one place. The factory changes not only where production occurs but how people organize shared time.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT: factory organization alone does not separately explain water, power and ports.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> Industrial location depends on water, power and logistics together because production inputs, operating equipment and moving goods must connect. An unreliable link can interrupt the production plan.</p><p>Water: verify the quantity, quality, continuity and discharge arrangements required by the process; cheap land alone does not make a site usable.</p><p>Power: check capacity and reliability, not only the tariff; outages can halt production.</p><p>Ports and logistics: assess connections to suppliers and customers, transit time and reliability; port delays can hold up inputs and deliveries.</p><p>This is a feasibility checklist, not site approval or an investment recommendation.</p><ol><li>List water, power and delivery-time needs for the proposed product.</li><li>Compare supply records, connection conditions and logistics quotes for each site.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Process needs, permits, utility records and route costs remain unchecked.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://ipp.unido.org/industrial-parks-guidelines/phase-two-planning-design-and-policy-framework">Phase two - Feasibility studies</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://documents.worldbank.org/curated/en/336371560797230631/pdf/Underutilized-Potential-The-Business-Costs-of-Unreliable-Infrastructure-in-Developing-Countries.pdf">Infrastructure reliability and production</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/transport/how-resilient-ports-can-mitigate-global-supply-chain-disruptions">How resilient ports can mitigate global supply chain disruptions</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>7. 商品供应 / 燃料化肥与食品 / 现代航运成本和延误 / 本地传递条件</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 远方战争如何传导到本地商品和运输成本？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 战争、危机与外部压力都会迫使系统重新配置资源，但它们作用的入口并不相同。战争集中动员，危机暴露内部脆弱点，外部压力则改变系统可选择的空间。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> BACKGROUND_ONLY: historical reconfiguration does not establish modern commodity-price channels.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 远方冲突可以通过商品供应和贸易路线传到本地：供应减少或航运受阻，会增加进口、生产和运输压力，再可能传到家庭支付的价格。</p><p>燃料和化肥变贵会影响食品生产，航线中断也会增加运输成本与延误；进口依赖较高的地方可能更敏感。</p><p>引用历史机制和案例，不声称当前某航线已中断或某商品必定上涨。</p><ol><li>先查具体商品来自哪里、使用哪些路线，以及是否真的出现供应或运输中断。</li><li>再看本地价格、库存与补贴，区分已经发生的影响和风险情景。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 本次冲突、商品、航线与本地传递幅度未实时核验。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/Blogs/Articles/2022/04/28/blog-africa-faces-new-shock-as-war-raises-food-fuel-costs">Africa Faces New Shock as War Raises Food and Fuel Costs</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/transport/how-resilient-ports-can-mitigate-global-supply-chain-disruptions">How resilient ports can mitigate global supply chain disruptions</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2022/12/09/global-food-prices-to-remain-elevated-amid-war-costly-energy-la-nina">Energy costs and food prices</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · How can a distant war affect local goods and transport costs?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> The First World War brought industrial capacity, state mobilization and imperial competition into a new density. Total war expanded the organizational reach of states over population and production, while the end of the conflict pushed several imperial systems into dissolution and succession.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> BACKGROUND_ONLY: historical reconfiguration does not establish modern commodity-price channels.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> A distant conflict can reach local prices through commodity supply and trade routes: reduced supply or disrupted shipping can raise import, production and transport pressures that may reach households.</p><p>Dearer fuel and fertilizer affect food production, while shipping disruption adds costs and delays; import-dependent places can be more exposed.</p><p>Historical mechanisms and examples do not establish a current route closure or an inevitable price increase.</p><ol><li>Identify the commodity origin and routes, then verify an actual disruption.</li><li>Check local prices, inventories and subsidies; distinguish observed effects from scenarios.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: The specific conflict, commodity, route and local magnitude are not verified in real time.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/Blogs/Articles/2022/04/28/blog-africa-faces-new-shock-as-war-raises-food-fuel-costs">Africa Faces New Shock as War Raises Food and Fuel Costs</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://blogs.worldbank.org/en/transport/how-resilient-ports-can-mitigate-global-supply-chain-disruptions">How resilient ports can mitigate global supply chain disruptions</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.imf.org/en/blogs/articles/2022/12/09/global-food-prices-to-remain-elevated-amid-war-costly-energy-la-nina">Energy costs and food prices</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>8. 先回答比较方法 / 比重、规模、就业、生产率、产业结构 / 年份定义价格口径 / 未查询实际差异不得排名</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界方法回答；不宣称已取得两国实际差异。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 马来西亚与越南的制造业能直接用一个数字比较吗？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 机器不会自动产生工厂。动力、设备、原料、劳动与管理需要在同一地点持续协调，才使集中生产成为一种组织方式。工厂改变的不只是生产地点，也是人们共同使用时间的方法。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> BACKGROUND_ONLY: factory organization is not a comparison method or evidence of country differences.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 不能用一个数字概括两国制造业。先确定比较的是经济中的比重、实际生产规模、就业、生产率还是产业构成；这些维度可能给出不同答案。</p><p>制造业增加值占 GDP 比重与增加值总额不是同一个指标；比重较高不自动意味着规模更大。</p><p>比较实际差异时，要统一年份、制造业范围和价格口径；现价金额、实际增长和就业份额不能互相代替。</p><p>已回答比较方法；此处未查询两国观测值，不宣称已证明实际排名或产业差异。</p><ol><li>先选一个要回答的比较维度，例如制造业比重或行业岗位。</li><li>再取马来西亚与越南同一年、同定义的数据；没有对齐前不排名。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 两国对齐的数值、行业构成与就业工资资料尚未查询。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/NV.IND.MANF.ZS">Manufacturing, value added (% of GDP)</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/datasets/gdp-and-non-financial-accounts.html">GDP and Non-financial Accounts</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · Can manufacturing in Malaysia and Vietnam be compared using a single number?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> Machines do not automatically create factories. Power, equipment, materials, labor and management must be coordinated continuously in one place. The factory changes not only where production occurs but how people organize shared time.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> BACKGROUND_ONLY: factory organization is not a comparison method or evidence of country differences.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> A single number cannot summarize two manufacturing sectors. First distinguish their economic share, production scale, employment, productivity and industry mix; these dimensions can give different answers.</p><p>Manufacturing value added as a share of GDP is not total manufacturing value added; a larger share does not automatically mean a larger sector.</p><p>To establish actual differences, align year, manufacturing coverage and price basis; current-price levels, real growth and employment shares are not interchangeable.</p><p>The comparison method is answered; country observations are not queried here, so actual rankings and industry differences remain unestablished.</p><ol><li>Choose the relevant dimension, such as manufacturing share or industry jobs.</li><li>Obtain aligned Malaysia and Vietnam observations for the same year; do not rank before alignment.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Aligned country values, industry composition, jobs and wages have not been queried.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/NV.IND.MANF.ZS">Manufacturing, value added (% of GDP)</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/datasets/gdp-and-non-financial-accounts.html">GDP and Non-financial Accounts</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>9. 融资价格与审批资格分开 / 固定与浮动/重新定价 / 收入债务信用因素 / 不推出个人概率</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界机制解释；不冒充本地数值。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 政策利率下降是否意味着每个人都更容易拿到房贷？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 利率变化会改变新增或重新定价借款的成本，从而影响家庭可用于日常消费的余量。固定利率贷款的本金与利息付款通常不会跟随政策利率立即改变；浮动贷款取决于合同指数、利差和重设时间。税费或保险也可能改变总付款。这是通用机制，不是本国本年的统计结论。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> MISSING explanatory paragraph; existing typed rate mechanism does not establish approval probability.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 降息可能降低新增或重新定价贷款的融资成本，但不等于每个人都更容易获批。贷款价格与能否通过银行审批，是两个需要分开核对的问题。</p><p>固定利率合同在固定期内通常不会因政策利率变化而立即改变付款；具体变化取决于合同和重新定价时间。</p><p>审批还会考虑收入、现有债务、资产和信用记录；较低利率不能自动补足收入证明或消除其他风险。</p><p>依据英国传导说明与美国资格因素作一般解释；不提供马来西亚审批概率或个案金融结论。</p><ol><li>查合同是固定还是浮动、何时重定价，以及实际费用后的报价。</li><li>向拟申请机构核对收入、债务和信用资料要求，不把美国例子当本地规则。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 具体国家、产品、银行标准和个人资料未核对。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/quarterly-bulletin/2024/2024/about-a-rate-of-general-interest-how-monetary-policy-transmits">Interest-rate transmission and mortgage pricing</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/does-my-credit-score-affect-my-ability-to-get-a-mortgage-loan-or-the-mortgage-rate-i-pay-en-319/">Mortgage eligibility and credit costs</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · Does a policy rate cut mean everyone can obtain a mortgage more easily?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> The currently verifiable material is not enough to explain this question. Specify the change, place or comparison you want to understand so the next source can be selected; an unrelated example will not replace your question.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> MISSING explanatory paragraph; existing typed rate mechanism does not establish approval probability.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> A rate cut can lower financing costs for new or repriced loans, but does not mean everyone can qualify. The price of credit and eligibility for credit must be checked separately.</p><p>A fixed-rate contract generally does not immediately change payments during its fixed period; the contract and repricing date matter.</p><p>Approval also considers income, existing debts, assets and credit history; a lower rate does not supply missing income evidence or remove other risks.</p><p>UK transmission and US eligibility guidance support the distinction; no Malaysian approval probability or individual lending conclusion is supplied.</p><ol><li>Check fixed versus floating terms, repricing dates and fees in the actual offer.</li><li>Ask the intended lender for income, debt and credit requirements; US guidance is not local law.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Country, product, lender standards and personal information remain unchecked.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/quarterly-bulletin/2024/2024/about-a-rate-of-general-interest-how-monetary-policy-transmits">Interest-rate transmission and mortgage pricing</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/does-my-credit-score-affect-my-ability-to-get-a-mortgage-loan-or-the-mortgage-rate-i-pay-en-319/">Mortgage eligibility and credit costs</a> · </p></details></article><article><h3>10. 公共趋势与个人条件分开 / 可比较方向 / 明确选择和后续观察</h3><p>工程判定：可直接使用的有界方法与下一步。</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 准备换工作时，怎样区分世界变化与自己的实际条件？</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> 文明结构最终会进入空气、住房、交通、工作、收入与生活成本。生活环境决定日常基础条件，就业把个人接入社会资源与职业路径，收入与必要成本之间的余量则影响家庭缓冲和转换能力。</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT for life conditions; the procedural comparison/review path supplies the practical next step.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> 先把世界趋势与自己的可核实条件分开，再比较方向。行业变化是背景；你的实际岗位要求、实得收入、通勤、照护时间和缓冲资金，才是判断某个选择是否可行的条件。</p><p>宏观平均数不能替代个人收入与生活成本；AI 任务暴露也不能直接证明你的岗位将消失。</p><p>这是整理与比较方法，不替你决定职业，不把预期写成已经发生的结果。</p><ol><li>在下方用合成或你自愿提供的资料比较两个方向，不自动保存。</li><li>选一个可观察条件，例如书面工时或实际通勤时间，事后复核。</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: 你的实际条件与后续观察需要你明确提供和核实。</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/indicators/average-annual-wages.html">Average annual wages</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.ilo.org/resource/article/how-might-generative-ai-impact-different-occupations">How might generative AI impact different occupations?</a> · </p></details><details><summary>en · When considering a job change, how can I distinguish world trends from my own conditions?</summary><p><strong>修改前 / Before</strong> Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change.</p><p><strong>原正文的实际支持</strong> PARTIAL_SUPPORT for life conditions; the procedural comparison/review path supplies the practical next step.</p><p><strong>现在 / Now</strong> Separate world trends from your own checkable conditions before comparing directions. Industry change is context; actual job requirements, take-home pay, commuting, care time and financial buffers determine whether an option fits.</p><p>Macro averages do not replace personal income and costs, and AI task exposure does not establish that your own job will disappear.</p><p>This organizes a decision; it does not choose a career or turn expectations into observed outcomes.</p><ol><li>Use the session below to compare two directions with synthetic or voluntarily supplied details; nothing is automatically saved.</li><li>Choose an observable condition, such as written hours or actual travel time, and review it later.</li></ol><p>仍未建立 / Still unestablished: Your actual conditions and later observations require your explicit input and verification.</p><p><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.oecd.org/en/data/indicators/average-annual-wages.html">Average annual wages</a> · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.ilo.org/resource/article/how-might-generative-ai-impact-different-occupations">How might generative AI impact different occupations?</a> · </p></details></article><h2>手机与桌面实际画面</h2><p>四张代表性最终截图，均为合成案例；没有删除历史截图。</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/final-en-1440.png">final-en-1440.png</a> · 173459 bytes</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/final-en-390.png">final-en-390.png</a> · 167733 bytes</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/final-zh-Hans-1440.png">final-zh-Hans-1440.png</a> · 315751 bytes</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/final-zh-Hans-390.png">final-zh-Hans-390.png</a> · 303329 bytes</p><details><summary>工程证据、模型费用边界与剩余能力 / Engineering evidence and remaining limits</summary><ul><li>原十题逐字保持，中英20问实际API与World/RIC链已运行；真实World四视口逐一显示十题并核对引用。</li><li>来源相关性、权限拒绝、篡改片段、复合论述缺证据、数值缺口、源码激活边界和旧版本选取均有负测；不是只检查排版。</li><li>Reality四组中英1440/390px实际完成来源查看/选择/撤销、处境比较、选择、后续自述观察、复核、刷新、撤销清空与失败清理。</li><li>来源版本变化测试仅证明本地冻结资料替代会使选取失效；不宣称自动发现远端官方修订。</li></ul><p>正文显示不再包含 SHA、JSON 路径、内部状态或开发诊断。技术证据只在本地人审/API审计输出中；来源失败与缺数值仍以普通语言告知，不以隐藏错误换 PASS。</p><p>复用现有 World 统计与公式、Ask 的正文解析及相关性 owner。新增的是本地有界论点组装及逐子命题来源联系，没有第二套 Ask、Reality、索引或数据库。官方来源说明只进入本地候选，不改变正式书稿或已接受知识权威。</p><p>独立 HTTP 对部分官方站点返回403，UNIDO一次网络失败，均保留；另一路官方网页／搜索原文已核对。引用摘要绑定的是本地选定片段，不是完整远端文档，更不代表实时修订监测。页面文案与来源联系仍等待 Human 审核。</p><p>KIR build admission 源码为 true，但现有运行路径要求两个环境开关及正式权限／费用条件；本轮未读取或更改生产开关。Ask 的 KNOWLEDGE_ENHANCED 仍拒绝直接开启。使用现有 gateway 的一次 fetch 替身模拟，真实Provider调用0。模型本身不能补缺失观测或承担来源权威。</p><p>实际费用授权仍为0。独立授权必须指定：任务、模型／Provider、输入与输出上限、调用次数、当前核实费率、最高USD及现有账户／商业owner的预算预留核销。900输出token上限来自现有gateway。费用公式为(输入token×输入每百万费率+输出token×输出每百万费率)/1,000,000；测试用虚拟费率和1500/900 token得到USD0.0033，仅算术示例，绝非当前报价或扣费。</p><p>源码保护：BaZi及World维护窗口原有4项变更逐字节核对；不修改其v10台账和测试。v10记录仍绑定旧候选，当前3项依赖摘要发生预期successor漂移，发布前须由原维护owner接续登记；本轮没有改旧hash制造PASS。未重跑无关全套冻结检查，不宣称发布门禁全绿。</p><p>现有World本地预览仍有未挂载的公共注册/视觉请求404及book6-runtime-readout 503；本轮通过的是回答与会话流程，不是全站、Atlas或生产可用性验收。既有地图、图谱与R2对象未删除。</p><ul><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/DELIVERY.json">DELIVERY.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/QUESTION-RESULTS.json">QUESTION-RESULTS.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/UNSEEN-RESULTS.json">UNSEEN-RESULTS.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/INITIAL-UNSEEN-RESULTS.json">INITIAL-UNSEEN-RESULTS.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/PRE-UNSEEN-SOURCE-HASHES.json">PRE-UNSEEN-SOURCE-HASHES.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/RELEVANCE-NEGATIVE-RESULTS.json">RELEVANCE-NEGATIVE-RESULTS.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/SOURCE-HTTP.json">SOURCE-HTTP.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/HTTP-VERIFICATION.json">HTTP-VERIFICATION.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/HTTP-EVIDENCE.json">HTTP-EVIDENCE.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/BROWSER-VERIFICATION.json">BROWSER-VERIFICATION.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/WORLD-BROWSER.json">WORLD-BROWSER.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/SAFETY-COMPILE.json">SAFETY-COMPILE.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/MODEL-SIMULATION.json">MODEL-SIMULATION.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/CANDIDATE-SOURCE.json">CANDIDATE-SOURCE.json</a></li><li><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59834/quality-r1/CHECKPOINT.json">CHECKPOINT.json</a></li></ul><p>停止于 HUMAN_REVIEW。Provider 0 / USD0；生产D1/R2写入0；资产删除0；commit/push/deploy 0。</p></details><hr><p>以下全部为历史人审记录，保留原文：</p></section><header><button id="language" type="button">English</button><p>PHI OS · RIC R1 · R0–R2</p><h1 id="title">让答案回到现实</h1><p id="subtitle"></p><p class="notice">LOCAL CANDIDATE · HUMAN REVIEW PENDING · NOT PRODUCT INTEGRATED</p></header>
 <section class="panel" id="world-reality-value-r1"><h2>World + Reality · Customer Value Recovery R1</h2><p><strong>LOCAL OPERABLE CANDIDATE · PARTIAL · HUMAN REVIEW PENDING</strong></p><p>先操作真实本地模块，再审查证据。未宣称开放问答整体成功、生产完成或 Founder 承诺已全部兑现。 / Operate the local product first; open-answer quality and production remain incomplete.</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:59833/world/?locale=zh-Hans">打开 World</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:59833/L1/PRODUCT-LOCAL.html?locale=zh-Hans">中文：提问与 Reality 完整流程</a> · <a href="http://127.0.0.1:59833/L1/PRODUCT-LOCAL.html?locale=en">English: question to Reality flow</a></p><p>启动：<code>node --import ./scripts/lib/pages-json-import-preload.mjs tools/review/reality-information-contract-r1/L1/server.mjs --serve</code>；新预览使用 59833，不占用旧 59832。</p><p>操作：自己提出公共问题 → 阅读部分解释并展开来源 → 在下方填写自己的问题、已知与未知、两个方向及条件 → 明确同意本次会话 → 比较并说明选择理由 → 记录后续自述观察 → 写复核与下次观察条件 → 刷新恢复 → 撤销清空。永久保存未授权、未实现。公共资料选取同意与个人处境处理同意分别控制。</p><p>实际实现：World 答案先行，来源与诊断折叠；复用现有 Ask 已发表正文解析与来源准入，逐段检索而非只显示文章目录；Reality 复用 PC、Navigation、RDG owner，数据只留本地会话。没有建立关系边，没有伪造可核实历史，观察与选择明确标为用户自述。</p><p>机器结果：十题 × 中英实际 API 与 RIC 链已执行；四组中英 1440/390px 完整浏览器流程通过；8 项权限/生命周期检查、5 项原 RIC HTTP 回归及 5 个局部编译通过。这些通过不能替代下面的回答质量判断。</p><p>World 原页面四视口已显示新答案与本地 Reality 入口；本地未挂载 book6-runtime-readout，仍返回 503，部分非本轮静态 owner 请求未挂载而为 404；未据此宣称全站/Atlas 视觉验收通过。现有 R2 对象和产品路径保留。</p><h3>十题实际回答质量 / Ten-question quality review</h3><article><h3>1. PARTIAL</h3><p>能源与运输的真实正文可支持背景；尚未充分解释食品价格的传导强度。 / Energy and transport context is supported; food-price pass-through is incomplete.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 油价上涨后，为什么连买菜和送货也可能变贵？</summary><p>全球化重新加速，需要运输标准、能源与制度同时支持。集装箱降低跨运输方式的转换成本，石油则为交通、工业与全球物流提供高密度能源，使远距离生产网络能够持续扩展。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-globalization-containerization-oil#article-body">全球化、集装箱与石油体系</a></p><blockquote>全球化重新加速，需要运输标准、能源与制度同时支持。集装箱降低跨运输方式的转换成本，石油则为交通、工业与全球物流提供高密度能源，使远距离生产网络能够持续扩展。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-energy-population-disease#article-body">能源、人口与疾病怎样改变文明条件</a></p><blockquote>文明的日常生活离不开能量。食物维持人体，牲畜提供牵引，燃料支持取暖和生产。一个社会能够获得、转换和调动多少能量，会影响它可以维持多少人口、劳动与设施，但能源本身不会替社会完成组织。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · Why can rising oil costs make groceries and deliveries more expensive?</summary><p>The reacceleration of globalization depended on transport standards, energy and institutions working together. Containerization reduced transfer costs across transport modes, while oil supplied dense energy for mobility, industry and logistics, allowing long-distance production networks to expand.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-globalization-containerization-oil#article-body">Globalization, Containerization and the Oil System</a></p><blockquote>The reacceleration of globalization depended on transport standards, energy and institutions working together. Containerization reduced transfer costs across transport modes, while oil supplied dense energy for mobility, industry and logistics, allowing long-distance production networks to expand.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>2. PARTIAL</h3><p>英文生活条件段落较直接；中文发展主义段落未充分解释工资分配，不能视为完整回答。 / The English living-conditions passage helps; the Chinese developmentalism passage does not establish wage distribution.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 工资没涨，经济增长的数据对家庭有什么意义？</summary><p>发展主义把经济增长、工业能力与国家建设连接起来，国家工业化则把资本、产业与基础设施集中到长期转型目标。相似工具在不同社会却产生不同结果。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-developmentalism-industrialization-outcomes#article-body">发展主义、国家工业化与不同结果</a></p><blockquote>发展主义把经济增长、工业能力与国家建设连接起来，国家工业化则把资本、产业与基础设施集中到长期转型目标。相似工具在不同社会却产生不同结果。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-environment-work-income#article-body">生活环境、就业与收入如何把文明带进日常</a></p><blockquote>宏观增长与个人体验不能自动画等号。相同就业率或平均收入之下，稳定性、可进入机会与必要成本仍可能非常不同。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · What does economic growth mean for a household whose wages have not risen?</summary><p>Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-environment-work-income#article-body">How Living Environment, Employment and Income Carry Civilization into Daily Life</a></p><blockquote>Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change.</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-developmentalism-industrialization-outcomes#article-body">Developmentalism, State-Led Industrialization and Divergent Outcomes</a></p><blockquote>Developmentalism linked economic growth, industrial capacity and state-building, while state-led industrialization concentrated capital, industry and infrastructure around long-term transformation goals. Similar instruments nevertheless produced different outcomes across societies.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>3. MISSING</h3><p>没有通过准入的资源富裕与发展机制正文；不得用系统维护等不相关段落填充。 / No admitted passage establishes the resource-development mechanism.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 矿产很多的地方，为什么就业和公共服务仍然薄弱？</summary><p>目前能核验的资料还不足以解释这个问题。先明确你想了解的变化、地点或比较对象，再找对应资料；我不会用不相关的例子代替。</p></details><details><summary>en · Why can a mineral-rich place still have weak jobs and public services?</summary><p>The currently verifiable material is not enough to explain this question. Specify the change, place or comparison you want to understand so the next source can be selected; an unrelated example will not replace your question.</p></details></article><article><h3>4. PARTIAL</h3><p>只有自动化/治理背景，尚未回答行业就业变化。 / Automation/governance context does not establish sector employment effects.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 如果企业开始用人工智能，我应该观察哪些就业变化？</summary><p>这里不宣称平台已经成为国家，也不假设人工智能必然取代人类治理。关键是观察哪些功能正在迁移、哪些决定需要可申诉与人类责任，以及快速模型如何保持可检查和可纠正。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-network-platform-ai-infrastructure#article-body">网络文明、平台文明与数据／AI 基础设施</a></p><blockquote>这里不宣称平台已经成为国家，也不假设人工智能必然取代人类治理。关键是观察哪些功能正在迁移、哪些决定需要可申诉与人类责任，以及快速模型如何保持可检查和可纠正。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book4-article-006#article-body">人工系统如何改变扩展的尺度边界</a></p><blockquote>技术推动扩展最深的作用，不是让现实失去成本，而是把某些高成本过程压缩成更低成本、可重复的结构。通信压缩距离，记录压缩记忆成本，标准压缩协商成本，自动化压缩重复执行，计算系统则压缩大量状态被读取和筛选所需要的人类注意。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · If firms adopt artificial intelligence, what employment changes should I watch?</summary><p>Technology&#x27;s deepest contribution to expansion is not the removal of cost, but the compression of high-cost processes into lower-cost repeatable structures. Communication compresses distance, records compress memory cost, standards compress negotiation, automation compresses repeated execution, and computation compresses the human attention required to scan large state spaces.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book4-article-006#article-body">How Artificial Systems Change the Boundary of Expansion</a></p><blockquote>Technology&#x27;s deepest contribution to expansion is not the removal of cost, but the compression of high-cost processes into lower-cost repeatable structures. Communication compresses distance, records compress memory cost, standards compress negotiation, automation compresses repeated execution, and computation compresses the human attention required to scan large state spaces.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>5. PARTIAL</h3><p>两种语言均能读取人口、劳动、照护机制；缺本地规模与时间估计。 / Both languages retrieve population, labour and care mechanisms; local magnitude and timing remain unknown.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 老年人口增加会如何改变家庭照护和劳动供给？</summary><p>人口压缩首先发生在年龄、能力与责任结构，而不是总人口数字。年轻节点减少、老年节点增加，会重新安排劳动、照顾、财政与知识更新之间的关系。当前经济与城市仍然可以依靠既有成年人、资本和技术维持，但真正变化的是未来节点进入速度：越来越多能力被用于维护已经形成的结构，能够投入下一阶段的余量逐渐下降。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book4-article-030#article-body">人口压缩为什么会首先变成关键节点的替代问题</a></p><blockquote>人口压缩首先发生在年龄、能力与责任结构，而不是总人口数字。年轻节点减少、老年节点增加，会重新安排劳动、照顾、财政与知识更新之间的关系。当前经济与城市仍然可以依靠既有成年人、资本和技术维持，但真正变化的是未来节点进入速度：越来越多能力被用于维护已经形成的结构，能够投入下一阶段的余量逐渐下降。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · How can an older population change family care and labour supply?</summary><p>Population compression begins in the structure of age, capability, and responsibility rather than in the headline population number. Fewer younger nodes and more older nodes rearrange labor, care, public finance, and knowledge renewal. The economy and cities may continue to function through existing adults, capital, and technology, while the real change occurs in the inflow of future nodes: more present capability is used to maintain what already exists, leaving less surplus for the next stage.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book4-article-030#article-body">Why Population Compression First Becomes a Problem of Replacing Critical Nodes</a></p><blockquote>Population compression begins in the structure of age, capability, and responsibility rather than in the headline population number. Fewer younger nodes and more older nodes rearrange labor, care, public finance, and knowledge renewal. The economy and cities may continue to function through existing adults, capital, and technology, while the real change occurs in the inflow of future nodes: more present capability is used to maintain what already exists, leaving less surplus for the next stage.</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-energy-population-disease#article-body">Energy, population and disease</a></p><blockquote>Population also means more than a total. Density, age structure, migration and arrangements for work change resource demands and forms of cooperation. More people can enable greater specialization while placing heavier pressure on land, food and public infrastructure. Numbers acquire meaning within a particular structure.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>6. PARTIAL</h3><p>工厂组织与投入协调有出处；水源、港口和电力的具体选址比较缺口保留。 / Factory coordination is sourced; water, port and power siting comparisons remain incomplete.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 为什么工厂选址要同时考虑用水、港口和供电？</summary><p>机器不会自动产生工厂。动力、设备、原料、劳动与管理需要在同一地点持续协调，才使集中生产成为一种组织方式。工厂改变的不只是生产地点，也是人们共同使用时间的方法。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-industrial-organization#article-body">工厂、城市与共同时间</a></p><blockquote>机器不会自动产生工厂。动力、设备、原料、劳动与管理需要在同一地点持续协调，才使集中生产成为一种组织方式。工厂改变的不只是生产地点，也是人们共同使用时间的方法。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-multiple-modernities#article-body">现代化为什么没有唯一答案</a></p><blockquote>铁路、学校、工厂、银行和现代政府越来越普遍以后，世界看起来开始使用相似工具。但工具相似，并没有使国家、资本与社会之间的关系变得相同。现代化没有结束分化，而是改变了差异所在的层次。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · Why does factory location depend on water, ports and electricity together?</summary><p>Machines do not automatically create factories. Power, equipment, materials, labor and management must be coordinated continuously in one place. The factory changes not only where production occurs but how people organize shared time.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-industrial-organization#article-body">Factories, cities and shared time</a></p><blockquote>Machines do not automatically create factories. Power, equipment, materials, labor and management must be coordinated continuously in one place. The factory changes not only where production occurs but how people organize shared time.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>7. PARTIAL</h3><p>历史战争与资源重组有出处，不能直接证明当前商品价格传导。 / Historical war and resource reconfiguration do not establish current commodity-price effects.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 远方战争如何传导到本地商品和运输成本？</summary><p>战争、危机与外部压力都会迫使系统重新配置资源，但它们作用的入口并不相同。战争集中动员，危机暴露内部脆弱点，外部压力则改变系统可选择的空间。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-war-crisis-external-pressure#article-body">战争、危机与外部压力如何成为重组器</a></p><blockquote>战争、危机与外部压力都会迫使系统重新配置资源，但它们作用的入口并不相同。战争集中动员，危机暴露内部脆弱点，外部压力则改变系统可选择的空间。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-colonial-order#article-body">殖民秩序与大西洋强制迁移</a></p><blockquote>征服能够夺取一座城市，却不能独自维持长期的资源获取。殖民秩序需要重新安排土地、征税、劳动、宗教与行政，使一个地方持续回应远方中心的需求。战争于是进入日常社会的组织之中。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · How can a distant war affect local goods and transport costs?</summary><p>The First World War brought industrial capacity, state mobilization and imperial competition into a new density. Total war expanded the organizational reach of states over population and production, while the end of the conflict pushed several imperial systems into dissolution and succession.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-world-war-one-and-empires#article-body">How the First World War Opened a Chain of Imperial Reconfiguration</a></p><blockquote>The First World War brought industrial capacity, state mobilization and imperial competition into a new density. Total war expanded the organizational reach of states over population and production, while the end of the conflict pushed several imperial systems into dissolution and succession.</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-war-crisis-external-pressure#article-body">How War, Crisis and External Pressure Become Reconfiguration Forces</a></p><blockquote>War, crisis and external pressure can all force systems to reallocate resources, but they enter through different channels. War concentrates mobilization, crisis exposes internal vulnerabilities, and external pressure changes the set of available choices.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>8. MISSING</h3><p>没有马来西亚/越南同口径产业数据；通用工厂段落不能算比较答案。 / Generic factory passages cannot substitute for aligned Malaysia/Vietnam data.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 马来西亚与越南的制造业能直接用一个数字比较吗？</summary><p>机器不会自动产生工厂。动力、设备、原料、劳动与管理需要在同一地点持续协调，才使集中生产成为一种组织方式。工厂改变的不只是生产地点，也是人们共同使用时间的方法。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-industrial-organization#article-body">工厂、城市与共同时间</a></p><blockquote>机器不会自动产生工厂。动力、设备、原料、劳动与管理需要在同一地点持续协调，才使集中生产成为一种组织方式。工厂改变的不只是生产地点，也是人们共同使用时间的方法。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-multiple-modernities#article-body">现代化为什么没有唯一答案</a></p><blockquote>铁路、学校、工厂、银行和现代政府越来越普遍以后，世界看起来开始使用相似工具。但工具相似，并没有使国家、资本与社会之间的关系变得相同。现代化没有结束分化，而是改变了差异所在的层次。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · Can manufacturing in Malaysia and Vietnam be compared using a single number?</summary><p>Machines do not automatically create factories. Power, equipment, materials, labor and management must be coordinated continuously in one place. The factory changes not only where production occurs but how people organize shared time.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book5-industrial-organization#article-body">Factories, cities and shared time</a></p><blockquote>Machines do not automatically create factories. Power, equipment, materials, labor and management must be coordinated continuously in one place. The factory changes not only where production occurs but how people organize shared time.</blockquote></details></article><article><h3>9. PARTIAL</h3><p>产品保留原有利率成本机制；没有个人审批概率或完整银行授信判断。 / The product retains the rate-cost mechanism; it does not establish personal approval probability.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 政策利率下降是否意味着每个人都更容易拿到房贷？</summary><p>利率变化会改变新增或重新定价借款的成本，从而影响家庭可用于日常消费的余量。固定利率贷款的本金与利息付款通常不会跟随政策利率立即改变；浮动贷款取决于合同指数、利差和重设时间。税费或保险也可能改变总付款。这是通用机制，不是本国本年的统计结论。</p></details><details><summary>en · Does a policy rate cut mean everyone can obtain a mortgage more easily?</summary><p>The currently verifiable material is not enough to explain this question. Specify the change, place or comparison you want to understand so the next source can be selected; an unrelated example will not replace your question.</p></details></article><article><h3>10. PARTIAL</h3><p>已有工作、收入、生活成本的背景解释；具体职业选择由用户在 Reality 明确比较和选择。 / Work, income and cost context is sourced; personal choices remain user-owned.</p><details><summary>zh-Hans · 准备换工作时，怎样区分世界变化与自己的实际条件？</summary><p>文明结构最终会进入空气、住房、交通、工作、收入与生活成本。生活环境决定日常基础条件，就业把个人接入社会资源与职业路径，收入与必要成本之间的余量则影响家庭缓冲和转换能力。</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-environment-work-income#article-body">生活环境、就业与收入如何把文明带进日常</a></p><blockquote>文明结构最终会进入空气、住房、交通、工作、收入与生活成本。生活环境决定日常基础条件，就业把个人接入社会资源与职业路径，收入与必要成本之间的余量则影响家庭缓冲和转换能力。</blockquote><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book4-article-045#article-body">文明为什么会失配，而治理往往最先落后</a></p><blockquote>文明失配首先是一种时间差。成熟文明的大量制度、城市、专业、资源网络与文化习惯都来自过去，它们能长期存在正因为曾经有效；问题发生在现实变化速度开始超过结构更新速度。人口已经老化，资源配置仍按旧人口假设运行；技术已经改变劳动，教育继续生产旧职业路径；城市流动方式改变，住房与交通却仍按过去结构分配。系统没有停止，只是结构与条件之间的对应越来越弱。</blockquote></details><details><summary>en · When considering a job change, how can I distinguish world trends from my own conditions?</summary><p>Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change.</p><p><a href="https://getphios.com/articles/book6-environment-work-income#article-body">How Living Environment, Employment and Income Carry Civilization into Daily Life</a></p><blockquote>Civilizational structures eventually enter daily life through air, housing, transport, work, income and living costs. Living environment shapes basic conditions, employment connects people to resources and career paths, and the margin between income and necessary costs affects household buffers and capacity to change.</blockquote></details></article><h3>Ask 的真实边界 / Existing Ask capability</h3><p>customer-contextual-ask.js 正常路径可返回 DETERMINISTIC_SOURCE_RETRIEVAL；同时现有 kir-r2-production.js、kir-r2-w16r2-successor.js、kir-r2-model-gateway.js 确实具备模型组织入口，并受 PHIOS_KIR_R2_MODEL_GATEWAY_ENABLED 及 production admission